  "status_text": "For one more family the cost without NOT gates is now known exactly at every size: on one-a-side inputs, an n by n graph whose rows are nested inside one another, one of them joined to every column, with exactly 3 distinct rows, needs exactly 2n - 1 - a - b AND/OR gates of fan-in two, where a is the number of rows with the fewest neighbours and b the number of columns with the fewest; the floor [L-meta-21908] and the ceiling [L-meta-19451, at k = 3] are both checked in Lean. Verdicts and merges are slower this hour; everything sent is kept.",
